  {# ── What this is ────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-display-xs font-semibold text-greyscale-900">What this is</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-greyscale-700 leading-relaxed">
      A citator surfaces how a court opinion has been treated by other opinions — reversed, overruled, criticized, distinguished, or simply cited. Lawyers use citators to gauge whether a case is still good law before relying on it.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-greyscale-700 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-greyscale-900">
      This demo previews the AI-powered citator that Free Law Project will integrate into
      <a href="https://www.courtlistener.com/" class="links" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CourtListener</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  {# ── At a glance (combined: features + reference) ────────────────── #}
  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-display-xs font-semibold text-greyscale-900">At a glance</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-greyscale-700 leading-relaxed">
      A few conventions and concepts worth knowing before you start.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-greyscale-500">Severity tiers</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">
      Every treatment rolls up into one of four severity tiers, most consequential first.
    </p>
    <dl class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[max-content_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-2.5 items-center text-sm">
      <dt>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide bg-red-500/10 text-red-700">
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM8.28 7.22a.75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06L8.94 10l-1.72 1.72a.75.75 0 101.06 1.06L10 11.06l1.72 1.72a.75.75 0 101.06-1.06L11.06 10l1.72-1.72a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06L10 8.94 8.28 7.22z" clip-rule="evenodd" /></svg>
          Stop
        </span>
      </dt>
      <dd class="text-greyscale-700 leading-relaxed">No longer good law for the proposition cited.</dd>

      <dt>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide bg-orange-500/10 text-orange-700">
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.485 2.495c.673-1.167 2.357-1.167 3.03 0l6.28 10.875c.673 1.167-.17 2.625-1.516 2.625H3.72c-1.347 0-2.189-1.458-1.515-2.625L8.485 2.495zM10 5a.75.75 0 01.75.75v3.5a.75.75 0 01-1.5 0v-3.5A.75.75 0 0110 5zm0 9a1 1 0 100-2 1 1 0 000 2z" clip-rule="evenodd" /></svg>
          Warning
        </span>
      </dt>
      <dd class="text-greyscale-700 leading-relaxed">Partially weakened but not entirely overturned.</dd>

      <dt>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-700">
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7 4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zm-1-9a.75.75 0 00-.75.75v3.5a.75.75 0 001.5 0v-3.5A.75.75 0 0010 5z" clip-rule="evenodd" /></svg>
          Caution
        </span>
      </dt>
      <dd class="text-greyscale-700 leading-relaxed">Intact but applicability is qualified.</dd>

      <dt>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide bg-greyscale-200 text-greyscale-700">
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM7 9.5a.75.75 0 000 1.5h6a.75.75 0 000-1.5H7z" clip-rule="evenodd" /></svg>
          Neutral
        </span>
      </dt>
      <dd class="text-greyscale-700 leading-relaxed">Stands; citation is informational or procedural.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-greyscale-500">Direct history vs. Citing reference</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">
      For every opinion, the citator identifies both the procedural history of the case and how later cases have treated it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-md border border-greyscale-200 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-greyscale-700">
        <strong class="block text-greyscale-900">Direct history</strong>
        <span class="block mt-1.5 text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">What happened to <em>this</em> case as it moved through the courts. Was it affirmed, reversed, vacated, or remanded on appeal? This is the procedural history of the case itself.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-greyscale-200 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-greyscale-700">
        <strong class="block text-greyscale-900">Citing reference</strong>
        <span class="block mt-1.5 text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">What later, unrelated cases said about the rule the case established. Did they follow it, distinguish it, criticize it, or overrule it? This is the signal for whether the case is still good law in practice.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-greyscale-500">Other things to notice</h3>
    <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-md border border-greyscale-200 px-3 py-3 text-sm text-greyscale-700">
        <strong class="block text-greyscale-900">Consistency across views</strong>
        <span class="block mt-1 text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">Each treatment is recorded once and surfaces wherever it's relevant — the same severity, label, and validation indicator appear on the search results card, the opinion-page summary, the Authorities tab, and the Cited By tab.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-greyscale-200 px-3 py-3 text-sm text-greyscale-700">
        <strong class="block text-greyscale-900">Supporting quote in context</strong>
        <span class="block mt-1 text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">Every Authorities and Cited By row expands to show the surrounding paragraph from the citing opinion, with the quote highlighted. On the Authorities tab, clicking the quote jumps to the Opinion tab so you can read it in full context.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-greyscale-200 px-3 py-3 text-sm text-greyscale-700">
        <strong class="block text-greyscale-900">"As recognized by" treatments</strong>
        <span class="block mt-1 text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">Used when the citing court isn't doing the action itself, but is acknowledging that another case has. Applied as a modifier (e.g., <em>Limited as recognized by</em>) that inherits the underlying severity.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-greyscale-200 px-3 py-3 text-sm text-greyscale-700">
        <strong class="block text-greyscale-900">Editorial validation marks</strong>
        <span class="block mt-1 text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">Three icons next to each treatment indicate whether the model's classification has been validated against the expert's classification — Validated, Invalidated, or Unvalidated.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

