      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-greyscale-600 leading-relaxed">
        Each negative treatment also has an "as recognized by" modifier (e.g., <em>Limited as recognized by</em>) — used when the citing court isn't doing the action itself, but is acknowledging that some other case has. The modifier inherits the same severity tier as the underlying treatment.
      </p>
